# Live Listen — publicly launched

Live Listen **is live for users** on `staging` and `main`. Do not set `NABAD_LIVE_LISTEN_PUBLIC_SHIPPED` back to false.

v1 is a **host-owned one-song session** (not a playlist). Host owns play/pause/seek. Guests follow the host clock. If the host has left, never autoplay — offer play from the start as a normal listen.

## Public launch

| Gate | Now |
|---|---|
| `NABAD_LIVE_LISTEN_PUBLIC_SHIPPED` in `src/feature-flags.js` | **`true`** — do not turn it off |
| Who can invite | Any signed-in user |
| Who can join | Anyone invited |
| Production API | `NABAD_LIVE_LISTEN_ENABLED=1` on nabadai.com |
| Staging API | on by default on Vercel Preview |

Before **every push to `main`**: `npm run verify:no-producer-ship` (Producer + Vibe + Edit must stay hidden).

## Daily workflow

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Normal fixes (simulator) | `git checkout staging` → `npm run sim` |
| Sami's phone — staging (Producer + Vibe + Edit + Live Listen) | `npm run run:ios:staging` |

## Agent rules

- **Do not** set `NABAD_LIVE_LISTEN_PUBLIC_SHIPPED` back to false.
- **Do not** remove Live Listen code to hide it.
- **Do not** start with live playlists / shared queues — keep v1 one song, one host.
- Production database already uses `supabase/listen_sessions.sql` (shared with staging). Apply `supabase/listen_sessions_guest_joined.sql` on production only if that column is missing.
